# Slice 284 probe: a prefix sign after a comma, `two(x, -y)` and `two(x, - y)`: two actuals or the binary minus?  Entry 7.
fn: two (int: a; int: b) int
    return: a * 10 + b
end: two
int: x 3
int: y 4
int: code 7
if: two(x, -y) != 26
    code: 11
---
if: code = 7 && two(x, - y) != 26
    code: 12
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
